Hexapod ROS 2 System — Docker Edition
=====================================

This repository packages the hexapod robot project for use inside a Docker
container. It is a derivative work of:

    Hexapod-ROS2-System
    https://github.com/Siedmiu/Hexapod-ROS2-System
    Original author: Bebo457 (Siedmiu) <bartekbab845@gmail.com>

All robot models (URDF/xacro), meshes, gait algorithms, hardware interface
and MoveIt configuration in `sim_and_real/` and `Sim Models/` are the original
work of the upstream author and remain under their respective licences, as
declared in each `package.xml`:

    hex_gz                  Apache-2.0
    hexapod                 Apache-2.0
    hexapod_description     Apache-2.0
    hexapod_hardware        Apache-2.0
    hexapod_moveit_config   BSD-3-Clause

The Docker packaging added in this repository (the `docker/` directory,
`install.sh`, `run.sh`, `docker-compose*.yml` and the rewritten `README.md`)
was added to run the project on ROS 2 Jazzy + Gazebo Harmonic in a container,
and is distributed under the same Apache-2.0 terms.

The initial setup and configuration patterns of the upstream project were
inspired by the ROBOTIS open_manipulator project
(https://github.com/ROBOTIS-GIT/open_manipulator).

Third-party components used at runtime, each under its own licence:
  - ROS 2 Jazzy Jalisco  - Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause
  - Gazebo Harmonic     - Apache-2.0
  - MoveIt 2            - BSD-3-Clause
  - ros2_control        - Apache-2.0
  - ros_gz              - Apache-2.0
